<title>FRANCE: SocGen declines comment on CIC.</title>
<headline>SocGen declines comment on CIC.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale declined comment on Thursday on a finance ministry decision to stop the privatisation procedure of regional banking group CIC.</p>
<p>&quot;We made no comment during the tender and we're not saying any more now,&quot; said a spokeswoman for the bank.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said earlier on Thursday that the privatisation procedure had been halted.</p>
<p>Arthuis said the privatisation commission had decided that a BNP offer complied with the sell-off conditions but an offer by Societe Generale had been rejected by the commission and that the sale procedure was therefore being halted.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newwroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
